{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips on both of its limbs on this driver's own record: EV-DPROF-00207 shows driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d of 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 61 is 11.5 percent, which is greater than the 8 percent rate. Compensation must therefore be withheld and the driver cannot collect anything for this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The clause reads the trailing-30-day counters, not the lifetime ones, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting one for the other: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 even though driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags is 0, and only the trailing-30-day figure may ground the anti-farming test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The tripping of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is itself an enumerated escalation trigger under POL-NS-09(d), and POL-NS-09 fires where ANY of its triggers holds, so escalation to a human reviewer is mandatory on this record and the automated pipeline issues no monetary ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal and the disputed cancellation fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded; EV-FARE-00207 already records payment_status PENDING with refund_issued_sgd of 0.00, so the rider is not made to carry the contested SGD 4.00 while the reviewer decides.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 directs the escalation packet to instruct the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, so the escalation carries a defined remedy rather than leaving the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line unresolved: that line is the sum the reviewer is directed to return.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own device track does not support the assertion that she came down: EV-GPS-00207 places her fixes about 1.9 km from the pin throughout the window with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0, and the rider does not press POL-NS-04, whose limb (a) requires a coordinating message the chat log does not contain. Rider presence is not an element of the escalation trigger, so the disposition of the fee turns on POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09, not on where the rider stood.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00207", "EV-GPS-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING, carrying issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT at weight 0.0 - no advisory covers Woodlands Ave 6 in this window - and its absence is itself citable: POL-NS-06(i) requires an advisory that is present and populated, so the accumulation limb cannot be run at all and the driver's dwell rests solely on the single qualifying in-geofence run of 507 seconds that EV-GPS-00207 measures.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00207-01", "EV-GPS-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"ESCALATE","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":["POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full, the fee being held rather than collected or refunded while review is pending."],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To the rider: your SGD 4.00 is not released by the automated pipeline, but the case goes to a human reviewer with a direction that the fee be refunded to you. The driver reached Blk 682 and held position inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup zone from 06:41:10 until he cancelled at 06:49:37 — 507 seconds, comfortably past the 300-second minimum — and he cancelled under RIDER_NO_SHOW. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 are met. Your account that you 'did come down, just a few minutes later' is not supported: your own phone's GPS places you about 1.9 km from the pin for the whole window, with 0 qualifying fixes near the pickup, and no locating message from you appears in the chat. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate you — you sent nothing coordinating, and the driver's in-app call at 06:45:10 went unanswered. POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance) is not engaged because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it, and POL-NS-05 is not engaged because the arrival marker was true — he was 14.47 m from the pin and stationary, not over 300 m away or moving at 15 km/h. On the merits the fee stood.

To the driver: your four limbs under POL-NS-01 are made out, and POL-NS-07 would have paid you 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, i.e. SGD 3.20, leaving SGD 0.80 as the platform service fee. That payment is withheld. POL-NS-07's anti-farming check is run on the two trailing-30-day counters your clause names, and it trips on both limbs: no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more), and 7 of 61 completed trips is 11.5 percent, above the 8 percent rate. Because the check trips, compensation is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). The disputed SGD 4.00 is held — the ledger already shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — and the escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund it to the rider. The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags (0) is not the field this test reads and was not used against you.

One further note: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), which makes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation limb unavailable. It is not needed here, because the driver's dwell is a single unbroken in-geofence run of 507 seconds, and the absence is not used against either party. All deciding artifacts (trip record, GPS trace, driver profile, fare breakdown) carry full weight 1.0."},"discarded_claims":[]}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: Direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The driving facts are not really in dispute once the telemetry is read. The driver reached Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6, and the GPS trace puts his vehicle 14.47 m from the pickup pin - well inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup - on unbroken 10-second telemetry carrying 52 consecutive qualifying fixes. He stayed inside that geofence continuously for 507 seconds, from 06:41:10 to 06:49:37, which is 207 seconds more than the 300-second STANDARD minimum, and he cancelled at 06:49:37 under RIDER_NO_SHOW. That satisfies all four conditions of POL-NS-01, and no rider-side clause displaces it: the arrival marker was not false (the driver was stationary at the pin, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or above, so POL-NS-05 does not fire), there was no waiting-period shortfall (POL-NS-06), and this is not a wrong-entrance or pin-ambiguity case - one registered pickup point, and the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than merely within 400 m of it (POL-NS-03). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider either: she posted no coordinating message, and the driver both messaged her and placed an in-app call at 06:45:10 that went unanswered. The rider's account that she came down a few minutes late is contradicted by her own device: 118 fixes, none of them inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, sitting roughly 1.9 km from the pin for the whole window. Nothing in the bundle is impaired under POL-NS-08 - clock skew, trace gaps, chat completeness and fare reconciliation are all clean - so her account is outweighed by her own trace rather than discounted. Ordinarily the charge would stand and the driver would receive 80 percent of it, SGD 3.20, under POL-NS-07, leaving the fee in place under NO_ACTION. But POL-NS-07's anti-farming check trips on both of its limbs on this driver's own record: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 over 61 completed trips in 30 days is 11.5 percent, above the 8 percent rate limb. Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09(d) - a profile-based anti-farming safeguard, not a finding that this rider was present at the block. The disputed SGD 4.00 is held, neither collected nor refunded, while review is pending; the fare ledger already shows payment_status PENDING with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the rider is not out of pocket in the meantime. POL-NS-07's anti-farming branch requires the escalation packet to direct the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, and that instruction is carried in the referrals. The open question the reviewer must settle is the anti-farming pattern on this driver's record - whether this and his other recent no-show terminations amount to fee-farming - and it is why a case that is otherwise decidable cannot be closed by the automated pipeline. Every artifact this ruling rests on - the trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown and driver profile - carries weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the platform floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"ESCALATE","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":["POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the disputed fee is held under POL-NS-09 pending that review."],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To both parties: on the trip itself, the driver's account is the one the instruments support. All four conditions in POL-NS-01 hold. The trip record shows a driver arrival event at 06:41:20 and the driver terminating the trip at 06:49:37 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding (limbs (a) and (d)). The GPS trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from 06:41:10 — ten seconds before the tap, so the waiting clock correctly runs from GPS entry, not from the tap (limb (b)) — and holds him there in one unbroken run of 507 seconds, 207 seconds beyond the 300-second minimum (limb (c)). POL-NS-05 (false marker) and POL-NS-06 (short dwell) therefore raise nothing, and POL-NS-03 is not engaged because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not merely within 400 m. Your account that you 'did come down, just a few minutes later' is not supported: your own device track sits roughly 1.9 km from the pin across the whole waiting window, and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate you because the chat contains no locating message from you and the driver's 06:45:10 in-app call went unanswered. On the trip alone the SGD 4.00 fee would stand and the driver would be owed SGD 3.20.

What decides this case is the driver's own record. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check trips on both of its limbs: 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days (4 or more) and 7 of 61 completed trips in 30 days, 11.5 percent, above the 8 percent rate. The clause requires the driver's compensation of SGD 3.20 to be WITHHELD and the matter to go to human review under POL-NS-09(d). That trigger fires, so the automated pipeline issues no money at all: the SGD 4.00 is HELD — the fare ledger already shows PENDING, neither collected nor refunded — and the driver collects nothing for this trip. Escalation is not a refund to the rider, and I am not awarding one here; but POL-NS-07 directs the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, and that direction is recorded as a referral. The SGD 4.00 belongs with the rider only once the reviewer acts; until then it is held.

On the evidence: the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00207-01, weight 0.0) is citable for its absence and makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, but nothing turns on it because the dwell was a single unbroken run. On the profiles I have used only the trailing-30-day counters the clause names; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags field is context only under POL-GEN-01 and grounds nothing."},"discarded_claims":[]}
